From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 13:59:28 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] Port the segment-reservation helper of aurora-silicon/m1n1
 aaf9fe96 (prerequisite of #47)

kboot: let the ASC firmware reservation skip segments outside DRAM

aurora-silicon/m1n1 #47 (J713 AOP handoff, ported in the next commit)
reserves the J713 AOP's DRAM firmware segments through
dt_reserve_asc_segments(..., dram_only = true), and extends
dt_set_aop_firmware(). aaf9fe96 ("kboot: Reserve the T6040 AOP's DRAM
firmware segments", Ryan Murray, on aurora-wip before #47) introduced
both. This tree has neither, so #47 does not build on it alone.

This commit ports only the helper half of aaf9fe96, unchanged:

  - dt_reserve_asc_firmware() becomes dt_reserve_asc_segments() with a
    dram_only argument. With dram_only it reads /chosen dram-base and
    dram-size from the ADT, and skips (with a log line) any segment
    whose 16 KiB-aligned span is not inside DRAM.
  - dt_reserve_asc_firmware() remains as a wrapper that passes
    dram_only = false. All existing callers are unchanged and keep
    their exact behaviour. The function body otherwise matches this
    tree's copy, including omacom's segment-list validation and the
    T6030/T8132 DCP os-log case (CODE: the region is byte-identical to
    a07d8c86^1 and a07d8c86, and differs from this tree's copy only by
    aaf9fe96's hunks).

Deliberately not ported: aaf9fe96's T6040/T6041 dt_set_aop_firmware()
and its call in kboot_prepare_dt(). They change T6040/T6041 behaviour,
which is outside the J604 work and untested on this tree. The #47 port
adds dt_set_aop_firmware() gated to T8132 only (see its message).

Fixtures: test_isp_optional.py, test_isp_reservation_full.py and
test_t8122_dcpext_ready.py compile dt_reserve_asc_firmware() out of
kboot.c, and now also need dt_reserve_asc_segments() plus a stub
ADT_GETPROP (only the dram_only path reads it). Their hunks are taken
unchanged from aurora-silicon 6b00c5f4 ("tests: follow the merged
kboot and NVMe code in the host fixtures", #44). After this change the
three files are byte-identical to aurora-wip's.

(cherry picked from commit aaf9fe9697c384cd0bc82458b9b97f817bcb88bd, partial: helper refactor only)

Hardware tested on: NOT YET
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
